46    write(11, "I've fully exercised the skill. Here's my assessment and the structured summary.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `add-social-media-header` skill is a **pure documentation/text-transformation skill**. It contains only two Markdown files (`SKILL.md` and `examples/README.md`) \342\200\224 no setup scripts, no executables, no network code, and no credential requirements. Its entire \"workflow\" is: take a README, insert a centered `<div>` block of shields.io badge images linking to social profiles, right after the title.\n\nI executed the complete workflow safely and locally:\n- Created a dummy README under `/home/appuser/workdir`.\n- Applied the skill's template, replacing every placeholder with dummy values (`DUMMY_CHANNEL_ID`, `dummy-user`, `dummy-channel`, `dummy-profile`, `dummy-handle`).\n- Validated against the skill's own rules: all four badges on a single line \342\234\205, `<div align=\"center\">` present \342\234\205, blank lines around the div \342\234\205, all-HTTPS URLs \342\234\205, no unreplaced placeholders \342\234\205.\n\nNote: the shields.io image URLs and social URLs are only *written into a file as text* \342\200\224 the skill never fetches them. Any network fetch would only happen later if the README were rendered by GitHub, which is outside this sandbox execution. **No network connections were initiated by me.**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"add-social-media-header\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Add a professional social media header (a centered div of shields.io badges linking to YouTube, GitHub, LinkedIn, and X profiles) to README/documentation files to improve engagement and visibility.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/add-social-media-header/SKILL.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/add-social-media-header/examples/README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la (skill dir and examples dir)\",\n    \"mkdir -p /home/appuser/workdir && create sample_README.md\",\n    \"Read sample_README.md\",\n    \"Edit sample_README.md (insert badge header block with dummy values)\",\n    \"cat -n + grep validation checks on resu"..., 3562) = 3562
